# Build context exclusions for a ROOT-context image build -- e.g. a release
# Dockerfile that compiles the kune binary.
#
# This file does NOT affect the dev container. Its build context is
# .devcontainer/ (see "build.dockerfile" in .devcontainer/devcontainer.json),
# which holds only a Dockerfile and a README, so it needs no ignore file.
#
# podman reads .containerignore in preference to .dockerignore. Only this file
# exists, so podman falls through to it -- do not add a .containerignore too,
# or this one is silently ignored.

# --- The big one: build output must never enter the context ---
# target/ is often gigabytes and would be rebuilt in-image anyway.
/target/
**/target/

# --- VCS and tooling ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.devcontainer/

# --- Editors / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Docs and local scratch: no effect on the binary ---
*.md
LICENSE*
docs/

# --- Secrets and logs: keep them out of image layers entirely ---
.env
.env.*
*.log
/logs/

# --- Coverage / profiling artifacts ---
*.profraw
*.profdata
/coverage/
perf.data*
flamegraph.svg

# Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, and src/ are deliberately absent from this file --
# a release build needs all three, and Cargo.lock is what pins the build.
